WEBVTT

00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:15,370
What do you think about S-O-T or D-T where they take your blood cells and

00:00:15,370 --> 00:00:21,770
tray them to attack your cancer? Yeah, we've had some patients go through S-O-T

00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:25,750
therapy. There's a clinic down in Florida. There's one in Arizona, I think it

00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:34,690
doesn't, and there's some in Mexico that do it. I don't know. I had one person

00:00:34,690 --> 00:00:39,130
recently that started it, did several sessions and then stopped, didn't think it

00:00:39,130 --> 00:00:45,850
was helping her, and I had somebody do it about two years ago. They thought it

00:00:45,850 --> 00:00:50,090
helped them, but they were doing so many other things too. I don't know how they

00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:55,610
could have discerned that. But, you know, I've heard good reports, so yeah, I've

00:00:55,610 --> 00:01:00,330
not against doing these, so a lot of these alternative things. Also, I cut out

00:01:00,330 --> 00:01:05,210
sweets and just about all sugar two years ago. Why is my hemoglobin A1C

00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:13,250
state about 5.6 and 5.7 in the past has always been lower. There's other factors

00:01:13,250 --> 00:01:18,970
with hemoglobin A1C, not just your sugar consumption, has to do with your

00:01:18,970 --> 00:01:24,090
cell membranes and healing your cell membranes, and that takes a lot longer time.

00:01:24,170 --> 00:01:33,330
It has to do with, you know, so your insulin receptors on your cell membranes don't

00:01:33,330 --> 00:01:38,770
change easily. So, and then, you know, would you increase insulin receptors on

00:01:38,770 --> 00:01:42,210
your cell membranes because of a bad diet for a long period of time? That's the

00:01:42,210 --> 00:01:47,210
problem with diabetes. Type 2 is that you got somebody with type 2 diabetes, and

00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:50,850
you think, oh, it's just an easy fix. You're just gonna go on a complete no sugar,

00:01:50,850 --> 00:01:56,090
no carb diet, and that's gonna fix your problem, and people can't figure out why

00:01:56,090 --> 00:02:01,370
it doesn't fix their diabetes. They still have elevated glucose levels. It's

00:02:01,370 --> 00:02:07,570
because you're damaged to your cell membranes, and as that cell replicates a new

00:02:07,570 --> 00:02:13,170
cell, it replicates a new cell with that same amount of insulin receptors on

00:02:13,170 --> 00:02:19,170
it. So, that's really the issue. It's a cell membrane issue, and it just takes a

00:02:19,170 --> 00:02:22,650
lot of time to move that needle.

